summary:
  What a device says about its error is passed on with the marks an address
  is made of, so a device that quotes the stream puts it into the line.

history:
  The failure line carries the device's own words now ("Resource not
  found"), and a device can put anything there. A station's address can
  hold a listener's token, and these lines are read into logs that get
  pasted into reports. The words are cut at the first character that is no
  letter, digit, space or one of , ' ( ) -, which leaves no room for a
  scheme, a host or a query.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
  _PLAIN_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 ,'()-]*")

replace:
  _PLAIN_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 ,'()/:.?=-]*")

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_fault.py::test_the_address_is_in_nothing_the_helper_says.
